## Description

When a hero has attack cards with different ranges (e.g., Cleric's "Righteous Advance" requiring adjacency vs "Sacred Flame" allowing attacks within 1 tile), the targetable monster list was incorrectly calculated using maximum range across all cards. This caused monsters within ranged attack range but not adjacent to appear in the targetable list, making adjacent-only cards show as unavailable despite monsters being "targetable."

## Changes Made

- Rewrote `getTargetableMonstersForCurrentHero()` to check each monster against each available attack card individually
- Monster now included in targetable list only if at least one available attack card can target it
- Added imports for `arePositionsAdjacent` and `isWithinTileRange` to GameBoard.svelte

**Before:**
```typescript
// If maxRange is 0, only return adjacent monsters (melee only)
if (maxRange === 0) {
  const tileId = getCurrentHeroTileId();
  return getAdjacentMonsters(currentToken.position, monsters, tileId, dungeon);
}

// Return monsters within the maximum range
return getMonstersWithinRange(currentToken.position, monsters, maxRange, dungeon);
```

**After:**
```typescript
// Check each monster against all available attack cards
const targetableMonsters: MonsterState[] = [];

for (const monster of monsters) {
  const monsterGlobalPos = getMonsterGlobalPosition(monster, dungeon);
  if (!monsterGlobalPos) continue;

  let canBeTargeted = false;

  for (const cardState of currentHeroPowerCards.cardStates) {
    if (cardState.isFlipped) continue;

    const card = getPowerCardById(cardState.cardId);
    if (!card || card.attackBonus === undefined) continue;

    const parsed = parseActionCard(card);
    if (!parsed.attack) continue;

    // Check if this specific card can target this specific monster
    switch (parsed.attack.targetType) {
      case 'adjacent':
        if (arePositionsAdjacent(currentToken.position, monsterGlobalPos)) {
          canBeTargeted = true;
        }
        break;
      // ... other target types
    }

    if (canBeTargeted) break;
  }

  if (canBeTargeted) {
    targetableMonsters.push(monster);
  }
}

return targetableMonsters;
```

